  That "over-advancement of a weapon school" can keep a wizard alive
early and middle.  Later is when wizards become unstoppable spell
casting machines.  That later includes XL:30 for skill slots, spell
casting efficiency, and mana.


  Other classes are different.  Usually classes will burn up a lot of
skill slots on #twoweaponing and the attendant weapon skills.  (Even if
#twoweaponing is limited to basic they'll waste skill slots getting the
primary and secondary weapons to Expert.)

 Attack spell skills are unlikely to be critical early.  (Magic missile
for a wizard doesn't need spell school advancement.  It also does damage
based on XL.)  Finger of Death probably can't be cast by an early wizard
no matter what the skill level, simply due to lack of XL and mana.
Magic missile is preferable for wizards over finger of death since it's
the wizard special spell, can be easily cast, and takes a lot less mana.
(Finger of Death probably isn't critical until meeting Rodney.)  Again,
Magic Missile does damage based on XL.  At XL 1 Magic missile averages
3.5 damage per hit.  At XL:30 with Int > 18 magic missile averages 56
damage per hit per monster, at range and reflectable.

  The real trick is to advance XL to 30.  Dancing with Foocubi is the
way to go.  That means increasing Cha by magic trap dancing, b!oGA,
rings of adornment, and cornuthaum (wizards).  Chaotic wizards can
summon major demons (including foocubi) by same race sacrifice.  A human
wizard with the portal to Ludios on the same level as an altar is in
great shape.  Lead the soldiers to the altar as self-portable sacrifices
with loot to identify.

  Even a plain sacrifest using the Eye of Aethiopica and the spell of
Create Monster for 20k turns can easily turn up enough foocubi to get to
XL:30, and beyond.  If you keep gaining experience from foocubi you
still get hp and mana gains even once you hit XL 30.  500 mana is not
difficult to get.

  But the whole secret is to use thrown Expert daggers to survive to the
point that you can develop into a full-fledged wizard.

